      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The main two chances have come out which completely changes this race. LADY CATALINA (2) is racing consistently in some good races, fifth in a pair of G3's at her past two starts. She was less than three lengths off Satono Glow two back at Flemington and that is outstanding form for this. Rates clear. HANDEE (7) was a dominant maiden winner first up then struggled out to 1200m at Ballarat. Don't mind her back in trip, she can improve sharply. MYHRO'S RULER (3) ran well over this trip at Seymour last time and can roll forward here. Right in this. SENZA NOME (4) won well enough fresh and could measure up.",
